STEP 4 — Backend source files and environment config

Files created:
- backend/.env
    The real settings file. Contains DB credentials and an empty
    GEMINI_API_KEY for you to fill in. This file is git-ignored (never
    committed) because it holds secrets.
- backend/.env.example
    A template with the same keys but no values. This one IS committed, so
    anyone cloning the project knows which settings are needed.

- backend/app/core/config.py
    Loads backend/.env (using python-dotenv) and exposes the settings:
    GEMINI_API_KEY, DB_HOST, DB_PORT, DB_USER, DB_PASSWORD, DB_NAME.

- backend/app/db/connection.py
    A small function get_connection() that opens a MySQL connection using
    the settings from config.py.

- backend/app/main.py
    The FastAPI entry point. Right now it only creates the app instance
    (app = FastAPI(...)). No routes/features yet, on purpose.

- Empty __init__.py files in app/, app/core/, app/db/ so Python treats
  these folders as packages.

Why this layout:
- It's the standard FastAPI structure: settings in core/, database in db/,
  app entry in main.py. It stays clean as features are added later.
